The brain wave finally came through. When a transaction happens, we will save the xwayland buffer so that the view remains consistent during transactions. However because the saved buffer replaces the real view disabling it, it will never send a wlr_surface_send_frame_done. This diff fixes the problem (but not a proper solution), however this might actually be a problem for wayland apps as well.

```
diff --git a/sway/tree/view.c b/sway/tree/view.c
index d664fe8d..f35b9bc0 100644
--- a/sway/tree/view.c
+++ b/sway/tree/view.c
@@ -1172,6 +1172,10 @@ void view_save_buffer(struct sway_view *view) {
                view_remove_saved_buffer(view);
        }
 
+       if (view->type == SWAY_VIEW_XWAYLAND) {
+               return;
+       }
+
        wlr_scene_node_set_enabled(view->content_node, false);
 
        struct wlr_scene_tree *tree = wlr_scene_tree_create(view->scene_node);
```

